WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:03.893
You read a fictional Azure
estate at four scopes,

3
00:00:03.893 --> 00:00:08.797
planned nineteen requests in order,
policies, then eligibility, then removals,

4
00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:12.267
saw each conversion add the
eligible assignment first,

5
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:15.738
and applied them to the fake
with nothing left to change.

6
00:00:15.738 --> 00:00:18.251
And you saw a read client refuse a write.

7
00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:22.562
Next is Module 7: access
reviews of privileged roles.

8
00:00:22.562 --> 00:00:25.647
The approval gate controls
the use of privilege;

9
00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:28.424
reviews control who keeps the eligibility.

10
00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:32.472
In Module 7 you define every
privileged review series as code,

11
00:00:32.472 --> 00:00:36.758
show a reviewer what a change will
do before it reaches the tenant,

12
00:00:36.758 --> 00:00:40.320
and hand the ISSO the
decisions each review produced.
